{
  "requirement": "The SDK offers this `InspectionContext` method and exposes it to the agent\nas the `outgoing_edges` command.\n\n```rust,ignore\nimpl<'d, D: Domain> InspectionContext<'d, D> {\n    /// Obtain this source's targets for the label.\n    pub fn outgoing_edges(\n        &self,\n        source: &D::NodeId,\n        label: D::EdgeLabel,\n    ) -> Result<Snapshot<Vec<D::NodeId>>, D::Error>\n    where\n        D::EdgeLabel: PartialEq;\n}\n```",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "The requirement has two structural obligations. Both are met.\n\n1. **The `InspectionContext::outgoing_edges` method.**\n   - `crates/habeas-sdk/src/graph.rs#impl[InspectionContext<'d, D>]/fn[outgoing_edges]` sits in `impl<'d, D: Domain> InspectionContext<'d, D>`.\n   - It takes `&self`, `&D::NodeId` and a `D::EdgeLabel` by value.\n   - It returns `Result<Snapshot<Vec<D::NodeId>>, D::Error>`.\n   - It carries the `where D::EdgeLabel: PartialEq` clause.\n   - This matches the required signature. The only difference is that the parameter is named `node` where the requirement says `source`. A parameter name is not part of the type signature.\n   - The body calls `label.clone()`. That compiles because `Domain::EdgeLabel` is declared `Clone + Send + Sync` in `crates/habeas-sdk/src/domain.rs#trait[Domain]/type[EdgeLabel]`.\n\n2. **Exposure to the agent as the `outgoing_edges` command.**\n   - `crates/habeas-sdk/src/agent/tools.rs#impl[GraphSession<'_, '_, D>/Conversation]/fn[tools]` defines a tool named `outgoing_edges`. Its parameters come from `edge_parameters::<D::EdgeLabel>(&path)`.\n   - `fn[dispatch]` in the same impl handles the `\"outgoing_edges\"` command. It resolves the node, deserializes the label into `D::EdgeLabel`, and calls `self.inspection.prepare_edges`. It then records an `OutgoingEdges` dependency and returns the target node paths.\n   - This is the command exposure the requirement asks for. `dispatch` is reached from the marked `tools` item, so it needs no separate marking.\n\nI found no structural gap and no conflicting element, and there are no `{fixme}` acknowledgments. I did not certify runtime behavior. That belongs to the separate behavioral requirements `outgoing_edges.behavior` and `outgoing_edges.inputs`.",
